A note on expert identity. Gemma-4-MoE has 128 experts per layer ; the parameters labelled 'E k ' at layer ℓ and 'E k ' at layer ℓ ′ are distinct FFN sub-modules. All specialty analyses below are therefore computed strictly within a single layer. Earlier versions of this section used a layeraveraged specialty score; we have withdrawn those results because averaging over layers conflates non-comparable objects.
For a fixed layer ℓ we compute specialty score s ( ℓ ) t,e = log ( p ( ℓ ) t,e / ¯ p ( ℓ ) e ) , where p ( ℓ ) t,e is the fraction of taskt routing events at layer ℓ that select expert e and ¯ p ( ℓ ) e is the cross-task mean at the same layer. We use layer ℓ = 12 (the peak cross-task differentiation layer, §3.3.2) as our running example. Table 5 reports the top-5 specialty experts per task.

